course: dictionary
lesson: 14059
title: Words that show learning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Mastered» is a word for learning something so well that you can do it easily. Look at the words around it to find the clues. «Once you have mastered times tables, you can answer quickly.» Times tables and answer quickly show that the learning is complete, so mastered means learned completely.
explain: «Mastered» can also mean you got control over a feeling or a difficulty. «She mastered her fear and climbed the rope.» The word fear tells you what she had to control, and climbed shows that she did not let it stop her. So mastered means got control over.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. In «He has mastered the piano», you can swap in «has learned well» and it still makes sense. Then try «has lost» and it does not, so you know your first meaning is right.
fact: Mastered is the past tense of master: master, masters, mastering, mastered.
fact: «Mastered» means learned something completely so that you can do it well.
fact: «Mastered» can also mean got control over a feeling or difficulty, as in «he mastered his fear».
fact: Common phrases are have mastered, mastered the art of, and fully mastered.
fact: In music, to master a recording means to make its final version.
exercise: «Once you have mastered times tables, you can answer quickly.» What does mastered mean here? | Lost in a game | Written on the board | *Learned so well that you can do it easily | Forgotten completely
exercise: «He mastered his fear and jumped into the pool.» What does mastered mean here? | Shared his fear with a friend | *Got control over his fear | Ran away from the pool | Made his fear grow bigger
exercise: Which word is the past tense of master? | mastering | masters | master | *mastered
test: «After months of practice, Sam has fully mastered the violin.» What does mastered mean? | Lost interest in the violin | Broke the violin | *Learned the violin so well that he can play it easily | Sold the violin to a shop
test: Which phrase fits the gap? «Mia ___ the art of drawing horses.» | *has mastered | has masters | has mastering | has master
exam: «The brave girl mastered her nerves before the big show.» What does mastered mean? | Watched the show from the back | *Got control over her nerves | Forgot all the words of her song | Lost her nerves completely
